config-connector-extensions patch 0007: mockgcp serves IAM workload identity pool managed identities and their attestation rules.

For iam.gcp.hfl.dev IAMWorkloadIdentityPoolManagedIdentity; applies on top
of patch 0006.
- mockgcp/apis/mockgcp/iam/v1/workload_identity_pool_managed_identity.proto
  is Config Connector pull request #14418's (head b080f5dc)
  mockgcp/apis/google/iam/v1/workload_identity_pool_managed_identity.proto,
  with the package changed to mockgcp.iam.v1, without the
  WorkloadIdentityPoolOperationMetadata that 0006's proto already defines,
  and, written here, with SetAttestationRules and ListAttestationRules (from
  the IAM v1 API) and the message mockgcp stores the rules in;
- generated/mockgcp/iam/v1/workload_identity_pool_managed_identity*.go are
  generated from it by hack/regen-mockiam-workload-identity.sh;
- mockiam/workloadidentitypoolmanagedidentities.go, written here, serves
  get, create (in an existing, active namespace), patch (description,
  disabled), soft delete, undelete, list, and attestation rules (set
  replaces them, at most 50); service.go registers it.
Upstream candidate: yes, with the PR.

